# Docker build context — the REPO ROOT for both images we ship:
#
#   docker build -f apps/hub/Dockerfile   -t maude-hub  .
#   docker build -f infra/cell/Dockerfile -t maude-cell .
#
# Until Cloud Phase 16 the hub built from `apps/hub` alone and used that
# directory's own .dockerignore. Widening the context (so the bundler can reach
# the single-source commit engine at apps/studio/sync/autocommit.ts) made that
# file inert — Docker reads ONLY the .dockerignore beside the context root. The
# first build after the change failed on a stale local node_modules being
# copied over a freshly-installed one, which is exactly the class of problem
# this file exists to prevent.
#
# The rule of thumb: exclude anything a maintainer's machine produces. An image
# must be a function of the committed tree, not of whoever ran the build.

# ---- never ship a maintainer's installed dependencies -----------------------
# Both Dockerfiles run a frozen install of their own; a local tree copied over
# it would silently substitute whatever versions this laptop happens to hold.
**/node_modules

# ---- version control + CI ---------------------------------------------------
.git
.github

# ---- build output the image regenerates ------------------------------------
apps/hub/dist
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources

# ---- local runtime state ----------------------------------------------------
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
apps/hub/data
.bun-cache
.kgai/store/graph.kuzu

# ---- deployment scaffolding, never part of an image -------------------------
**/docker-compose*.yml
**/Caddyfile
**/fly.toml
**/.dockerignore
**/Dockerfile

# ---- secrets. Belt and braces: these are gitignored, but a build context is
# read from the WORKING TREE, so a gitignored file is still in scope here. ----
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars.*
**/*.pem
